From 6412ae0458df450aae33bcf6e2b2da6e9773e910 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: davmels <davmelous@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:28:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] forensics: report non-finite gradients and logprob spikes

A NaN from Megatron's gradient check says only which rank and which iteration failed, so job 1190668 left no way to tell a few bad elements from a broken forward pass. When train fails on that check, write how many gradient elements are bad and in which parameters, and save the batch that rank was training on. NRL_FORENSICS_TEST_NAN=<n> poisons one gradient on the n-th train call to exercise this in a debug run.

Tokens whose log-probability moves by 10 or more between get_logprobs and training are also reported, at most three per microbatch, with the generation, get_logprobs and training values. The ratios are already computed for the metrics, so a step without a spike does no extra work.
